{"kind":"assert","text":"Independent complete read-only assessment of design c8318a8a06bf88e7ee1422c4ce99c34f602a439f, tree 5a4fe61fb5feaf27b18a7d56b0b784a7142d2a25. Existing clone/version design ownership remains. This is preflight feedback while normal owned evidence binding and invitation are pending, not a guarded verdict, contract adoption, source approval or implementation closure.\n\nRoot personally read all 35,987 bytes / 472 LF of the current note and all 15,344 bytes / 175 LF of its complete native U3 against b26, in seven bounded gap-free displays with both EOFs. Both independent reviewers also freshly read these subjects at c831. No predecessor or equal-blob body credit is used. Body SHA256: 4e29c2cd30263ffe138d66cdfb8e4e9d49a4a6198db24a96dde201e7ae877ab9. U3 SHA256: d9482f0444a2cdaa4348606b3010340e2f3dcb0af00a397b6600cefa0c8653ca. Unique subject coverage is 51,331 bytes / 647 LF. Only this note changes from b26; source/tests/configuration/history do not change. Root read both sealed peer reports and checked its actual ledger against the captured raw subjects.\n\nConclusion: the earlier 7229 provenance/current-authority findings remain answered, and the precise physical-send retirement gap in 75d620 is now resolved at the proposed invariant/state level. No remaining conceptual blocker is established in the complete current proposal. Concrete executor proof and owner adoption are deliberately prerequisites, not current runtime capability claims. A normal complete DESIGN verdict can now assess this exact subject once its correct owned binding is filed; this assertion does not substitute for that verdict.\n\nArchitecture and security: V1a preserves pure historical judgment under archived facts/time and separates it from current read/admission/provider guards. It does not issue present sessions, activate archived Workers or promote historical grants. Current full-reference, typed-resource, strict43d, clock, freshness, actual serving/standing and post-await checks remain conjunctive. Semantic refusal retains the actual contract behavior after access/provenance/activation preflight. The explicit operator bootstrap proposal has a pinned trust identity, complete scope allowlist, purpose and byte/signature/address/expiry limits, returns no custody/tokens, and cannot derive authority from unresolved membership. It requires adoption; otherwise acquisition remains incomplete.\n\nStable service identity, immutable admission release/build and current runtime release stay distinct. Signed canonical registry revisions bind service/parent/manifest/publisher, with configured operator anchors, controlled rotation/reset, monotonic floors and explicit local-manifest trust. Remote transport or replay success cannot replace executable correspondence. V4 coverage ends at exact witnessed heads and verified ancestry; later coverage needs a signed exact-head/continued-bundle/admission-build amendment. Mixed histories are preserved unresolved without guessing intervals, rewriting genesis or replacing an old room with fresh @2 success. Those are honest coverage and trust limits, not evidence that every old room already operates.\n\nH3 keeps immutable original-attempt scope/incarnation/origin/operation, semantic bundle, register/provider/account/installation/namespace/repository and capability/ref/lifetime. Dispatch, recovery, replies, credential retrieval and cleanup retain that original binding. Secret rotation cannot expand provider rights. H4 activates one coherent service/generation/runtime/registry/routing/bundle/port tuple, with per-operation convergence; a deployment label or stale config is not proof of activation.\n\nThe new physical-send rule excludes the previously ambiguous state. Admission tickets have their own authenticated commit/abort finalization. A physical send permit separately binds one durable dispatcher owner, fresh nonce, runtime release and original attempt/binding. Before markSent, abort requires a fence preventing later mark or call. At markSent, responsibility becomes irreversible and the attempt is conservatively may-have-started even if the RPC has not begun. That mark does not retire the permit, and crash-before-call does not authorize abort-to-unsent or original resend.\n\nAt the actual mutating boundary, including nested adapter continuations, current authority/custody/freshness and open permit/owner/nonce/release/tuple must be checked after awaited preparation. A closed continuation cannot cross a later asynchronous gap unchecked. The permit remains outstanding until authenticated durable closure/fencing excludes every continuation that could still invoke the original mutation, including repeat invocation after entry. A closed row, silent object, timeout or expired lease is expressly insufficient. Activation waits for admission finalizations and those actual local ownership closures. Remote outcomes need not finish after no local original call can start; ambiguity, late replies, custody and recovery/cleanup duties survive under the original binding and complete compatible successor tuple.\n\nThe concrete executor/transaction/port owners must identify and prove that fence across suspended/nested continuations and restart. An unsupported executor blocks retirement and activation rather than pretending quiescence. This proposal does not prove remote exactly-once completion, instantaneous session/token recall, atomic provider RPC transactions or an implemented fence. Existing original-attempt recovery semantics are preserved. Old releases without the barrier need actual replacement/drain evidence. Rollback uses a new monotonic generation and the same admission/closure duties, never dropped roots, lowered floors or an older incompatible binary.\n\nScalability and simplification: the existing capacity owner now explicitly owes issue/finalize transaction costs, peak outstanding admission/send permits, recovery backlog, durable abort/nonce/fence exclusion, runtime overlap, registry/root/reference-closure and archive bytes. Root count alone does not bound coordinator load. Backpressure may refuse new work, never discard issued permits or old duties. Numeric readiness and the candidate sixteen-root bound remain unadopted/unmeasured. Establish the consistency domain before sharding; throughput cannot weaken exclusion. Keep a narrow archive/evaluator and explicit attempt ports rather than a general provider registry, new effect engine or duplicate matrix. The conservative refusal/hold costs are visible; schedule estimates waive none of the remaining functionality.\n\nRemaining work is explicit: operator/security/contract adoption, authentic old/new scope/incarnation/genesis/head/build/source receipts and retained closure, canonical schemas, compatible executable/port correspondence, concrete executor proof, capacity evidence, then implementation and the existing focused/gate/live witnesses. These are requirements for the later owners; this note supplies no completed receipts or operational proof. Producer statements that their Root read/chose the note are producer attribution, not checker adoption. No source or provider approval transfers from the separately landed Gate1/live-operations milestones.\n\nActivity: immutable native Git, static complete text/report reading, raw hash/count/JSON checks and scratch evidence only. No project execution/import/eval, generated histories/canonical/Git vectors, tests/gate/compiler/install/audit, provider/private/process/browser probes, source edits, merge/push or adoption. Root owns the independent assessment; lead owns order and existing producers own implementation.\n"}